        }
      ],
      "text": "Brand compliance is the gate that determines whether a campaign draft meets required standards before scheduling."
    },
    {
      "claimId": "c-013",
      "component": "exemplar",
      "groundedIn": [
        {
          "id": "36839105-9fcc-4a84-a6ee-d2f3c29e4ae7",
          "kind": "decision",
          "summary": "score_subject_lines"
        },
        {
          "id": "03d52b64-7f83-41fb-ad2e-82e559edde66",
          "kind": "decision",
          "summary": "check_brand_compliance"
        },
        {
          "id": "9535fc32-9c42-405c-aee1-9cd378a0baef",
          "kind": "message",
          "summary": "The tidewatch 0.9 launch email is scheduled and logged.\n\n**What was sent where**\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Segment | Pipeline operators, 1,300 recipients |\n| Send time | 2026-10-16 09:00 UTC |\n| Subject | Per-topic lag alerts for riverbed, now in tidewatch 0.9 |\n| Draft | draft-camp-2026-10-003-02 |\n| Schedule ID | send-b5932c43 |\n| Notion log | log-0003 |\n\n**Decisions made along the way**\n\n- **Classification raised nothing.** The brief classified as a launch with full confidence, urgency 2, no legal review, and an empty review list.\n- **First draft failed compliance.** The Labs disclaimer was paraphrased instead of verbatim, and the call-to-action check sat at 0.53 with a review flag because I had split the ask into a reply request and a separate link. I rewrote it with the exact disclaimer and the brief's CTA as a single bolded link. The revised draft passed all four checks with no review items.\n- **Subject line chosen by ranking.** On the final draft the scorer picked the per-topic lag alerts line on composite score, well ahead of the other two. It flagged the runner-up's curiosity score for review at 0.54 confidence. I kept the scored pick, since the uncertainty was on a line already trailing by enough that a one-level swing could not overtake it.\n- **Scheduling happened only after the pass.** The first draft was never submitted for sending.\n\nOne thing worth a glance before the 16th: the third subject line mentioned \"30 seconds\", which is close to the banned unpublished benchmark category. It was not chosen and compliance did not object, but I would avoid that phrasing in future drafts."
        }
      ],
      "text": "In the tidewatch 0.9 launch, the ranked subject about per-topic lag alerts was retained after review of a losing line, and the compliant draft was scheduled only after the revised compliance pass."
    },
    {
      "claimId": "c-014",
      "component": "exemplar",
      "groundedIn": [
        {
          "id": "d29606e8-4dbc-4ef8-98c8-96d622012e53",
          "kind": "decision",
          "summary": "check_brand_compliance"
        },
        {
          "id": "06aa6f36-850d-470a-9bf3-afc0aba8916b",
          "kind": "decision",
          "summary": "check_brand_compliance"
        },
        {
          "id": "c8e2e227-2602-4a1e-916a-f2b5992c1c09",
          "kind": "message",
          "summary": "The ballast 0.4 launch email is scheduled to the CI builders segment for 2026-10-17 at 09:00 UTC and logged in Notion.\n\n**What went out**\n\n- Segment: CI builders, 900 recipients, platform-lead persona.\n- Subject line, chosen by the scored ranking: \"ballast 0.4: fail the build when p99 breaks your latency budget\".\n- Body covers the three key messages from the brief, one CTA to add the action to one workflow and open an issue, and the Labs disclaimer verbatim.\n\n**Decisions on review_required items**\n\n- **Legal review** flagged as uncertain by the classifier, leaning no. I decided no review. The brief has no pricing, competitor, regulatory, or guarantee language, and the 50x replay figure is one of the brief's own key messages. I kept the copy strictly to those messages.\n- **Subject-line scores** flagged five low-confidence sub-scores. The ranking was stable across two scoring runs with a clear margin, and the uncertainty ranges on the winner could not reorder it, so I took the ranked pick.\n\n**Compliance** failed once on the first draft because I paraphrased the Labs disclaimer. The second draft used the exact required text and passed all four checks. Nothing was scheduled until that pass.\n\nThe Notion campaign log entry records the schedule, both draft ids, and the reasoning above."
        }
      ],
      "text": "In the ballast 0.4 launch, the exact disclaimer and a single CTA were used after the first compliance failure, then the ranked subject was scheduled and the decisions were logged."
    },
